---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Icons reGospeled, a gospel that heals">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="stitle" id="top-heading" tabindex="-1">Honest theology, psychology, and community for worn down people.</h1>
      <p class="lead">You are a living icon, made in God's image, beloved and being made whole in Christ. Rediscover a gospel that heals, find your people, and begin with the book that meets you where you are.</p>
      <div class="cta-row center">
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/reading-finder/">Find your book →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-icon" href="#gatherings">Get connected today<svg class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14"/><path d="m6 13 6 6 6-6"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt" data-reveal>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <h2 class="stitle">If this is you</h2>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p>You went looking for something both theologically serious <em>and</em> non-shaming, and couldn't find it. Underneath is the exhaustion, the disillusionment, and the quiet fear that maybe the problem is you.</p>
      <p>It isn't. Fear-based, shame-based religion has always struggled to tell the truth about a God who is, first and last, love. The gospel was supposed to be good news, a Physician, not a scorekeeper.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- before/after gospel contrast (drag to compare) -->
  <section data-reveal>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <h2 class="stitle">Which gospel were you handed?</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="ba">
        <div class="ba-after"><div class="ba-inner">
          <div class="ba-col ba-scripture">
            <span class="ba-tag">Closer to the Greek &amp; Hebrew</span>
            <div class="ba-verses">
              <div class="v"><b>John 12:32</b><span>“I will <em>drag</em> all people to myself.”</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Galatians 2:16</b><span>Freed by the <em>faith of</em> Christ.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 6:5</b><span>Grown together as <em>one</em> with Christ.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Isaiah 53:10 · LXX</b><span>The Lord willed to <em>cleanse</em> him.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 3:25</b><span>The <em>mercy seat</em>, where God meets us.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ba-col ba-summary ba-summary-right">
            <span class="ba-tag">The gospel that heals</span>
            <ul><li>A Father, running toward you</li><li>A Physician, not a courtroom</li><li>Healing of the whole person</li><li>Love, first and last</li><li>You, a living icon, restored</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="ba-before"><div class="ba-inner">
          <div class="ba-col ba-summary">
            <span class="ba-tag">The God you were handed</span>
            <ul><li>A scorekeeper, arms crossed</li><li>A courtroom, always in session</li><li>Fear as the engine</li><li>Wrath, first and last</li><li>You, a problem to manage</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="ba-col ba-scripture">
            <span class="ba-tag">As it was handed</span>
            <div class="ba-verses">
              <div class="v"><b>John 12:32</b><span>“I will <em>draw</em> all people to myself.”</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Galatians 2:16</b><span>Freed by your <em>faith in</em> Christ.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 6:5</b><span>Planted together with him in death.</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Isaiah 53:10</b><span>“It pleased the Lord to <em>crush</em> him.”</span></div>
              <div class="v"><b>Romans 3:25</b><span>A <em>propitiation</em>, appeasing wrath.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div></div>
        <div class="ba-divider"><span class="ba-knob" aria-label="Drag to reveal the Scriptures"><span class="ki">⟺</span></span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="ba-hint">Drag the bar to reveal the Scriptures</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-reveal>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <h2 class="stitle">You're not crazy for wanting more</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
      <p>Icons reGospeled sits at the intersection of ancient theology, modern psychology, and relational presence. We read the Church Fathers and take the brain and the body seriously, because healing is a whole-person thing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fathers" data-reveal aria-label="Church Fathers we read with">
    <p class="label">We read with the ancients</p>
    <div class="fathers-track">
      <span>Irenaeus of Lyons</span><span>Athanasius</span><span>Basil the Great</span><span>Gregory of Nyssa</span><span>Gregory Nazianzen</span><span>Maximus the Confessor</span><span>John Chrysostom</span><span>Origen</span><span>Irenaeus of Lyons</span><span>Athanasius</span><span>Basil the Great</span><span>Gregory of Nyssa</span><span>Gregory Nazianzen</span><span>Maximus the Confessor</span><span>John Chrysostom</span><span>Origen</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="divine" data-reveal>
    <div class="trinity" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 200"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.4"><circle cx="100" cy="72" r="46"/><circle cx="76" cy="118" r="46"/><circle cx="124" cy="118" r="46"/></g></svg></div>
    <div class="narrow" style="text-align:center;">
      <h2 class="stitle">You are already beloved</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
      <p class="lead">You were never the problem. In Christ you are being made whole, already held, already home. Here the gospel becomes good news again, the whole person heals, and you belong to people who think deeply and love well.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt" id="begin" data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="stitle" style="text-align:center;">Ways to begin</h2>
      <div class="rule center"></div>
      <div class="grid begin-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/reading-finder/"><div class="tag">Free · start here</div><h3>The Book Finder</h3><p>Three questions, two books chosen for where you are, and a curated library of 60+ more.</p><span class="go">Find your book →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="/podcast/"><div class="tag">Podcast</div><h3>Less Heresy Than Expected</h3><p>Warm, witty, theologically serious conversation for believers, doubters, and the disillusioned.</p><span class="go">Listen →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="#gatherings"><div class="tag">Gatherings</div><h3>Come to the table</h3><p>Wings, Whiskey &amp; the Word, Movies for Humans, retreats, and a monthly reading group.</p><span class="go">See gatherings ↓</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="/course/"><div class="tag">Course · $20</div><h3>The Gospel You Were Never Told</h3><p>What if the Good News is actually better than you were told? Five sessions to find out.</p><span class="go">Take the course →</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="https://strengthenedbygrace.substack.com/"><div class="tag">Substack</div><h3>Strengthened by Grace</h3><p>Theological reflection, gospel interpretation, and spiritual restoration, free to read.</p><span class="go">Subscribe →</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="lead begin-promise">Our promise: we won't shame you, rush you, or hand you slogans. We'll meet you with depth, honesty, and welcome.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="gatherings" class="gatherings" data-reveal aria-labelledby="gatherings-title">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="stitle" id="gatherings-title">Come to the table</h2>
        <p>Grace, attentiveness, and real human connection. Bring your questions, wounds, hopes, and stories, and be known without being shamed. Belong before you believe it all.</p>
        <ul class="features">
          <li><h3>Wings, Whiskey &amp; the Word</h3><p>Every other week. Shared meals and honest conversation about theology, psychology, and the stories we carry.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Movies for Humans</h3><p>Monthly. A thoughtful film, a meal, and real discussion.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Theology Commons</h3><p>Monthly on Zoom. A reading and discussion group on Ultimate Restoration.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Men's Retreat</h3><p>Time set apart for worship, rest, and real brotherhood.</p></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/community/">See all gatherings →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <img class="photo-hero" src="/assets/photos/gathering-1.jpg" alt="Friends gathered around the table for Wings, Whiskey and the Word" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1067">
    </div>
  </section>

  <a class="to-top" slot="after-footer" href="#top" aria-label="Back to top">
    <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 19V5"/><path d="m6 11 6-6 6 6"/></svg>
  </a>

  <script>
    // Back-to-top: shows once the visitor is ~80% down the page.
    const btn = document.querySelector('.to-top');
    if (btn) {
      const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
      const update = () => {
        const h = document.documentElement;
        const max = h.scrollHeight - h.clientHeight;
        btn.classList.toggle('show', max > 0 && h.scrollTop / max >= 0.8);
      };
      addEventListener('scroll', update, { passive: true });
      addEventListener('resize', update);
      update();
      btn.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: reduce.matches ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
        // move keyboard / screen reader focus back to the top of the page
        const top = document.getElementById('top-heading');
        if (top) top.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      });
    }
  </script>

</Base>
